    kind: work_item  # 94ca
    title: "smart-test: order the local run failure-first (coverage-directed tests first) instead of dropping tests"  # 94ca
    status: todo_soft  # 94ca
    priority: 3  # 94ca
    parent:  # 94ca
    tags:  # 94ca
    - smart_test  # 94ca
    - ci_infrastructure  # 94ca
    isbefore: []  # 94ca
    duplicate_of: []  # 94ca
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 94ca
    pr_ref:  # 94ca
    description: "Idea (owner-approved to file, 2026-11-10; not measured): instead of REMOVING tests from the local run (--narrow), ORDER them. Run first the tests the coverage index saw executing the changed blocks, then the citation-gate tests, then the rest of the selection. Nothing is dropped, so neither the whole-tree text readers (WI-zajuv measurement: 69 test files) nor import-time code (WI-zunug) can cause a miss, and the CI manifest is untouched.\n\nLimit, stated up front: a green run takes as long as today. The gain is time-to-first-failure only.\n\nOpen questions to measure before building: how pytest-xdist distributes an ordered list (ordering may be lost across workers); how often a failing local run's first failure is in the coverage-directed set (the smart-test bed, scripts/smart-test-bed, can score this: for each edit, the rank of the first MUST test).\n\nDone when: measured on the bed, and either shipped with the rank numbers or closed with the reason it does not help."  # 94ca
    fields: {}  # 94ca
- op: discuss  # 4c72
  at: '2026-11-11T01:16:00Z'  # 4c72
  by: agent  # 4c72
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4c72
  clock: 2  # 4c72
  nonce: 4c72  # 4c72
  message: "Owner suggestion 2026-11-10 (hunch, not measured): after the first test failure, keep running for about 15 seconds to collect nearby failures, then stop, instead of running the whole selection to the end. Applies to the CI pytest step as well as local runs. Notes: pytest has only count-based stops (-x, --maxfail=N), so this needs a small plugin (record the time of the first failed report; once the grace period passes, set session.shouldstop; under xdist do it on the controller). Risk to measure: a truncated failure list can cost a second CI round trip when an unrelated later failure was cut off; failure-first ordering lowers that risk, so the two belong together. Measure on past red CI runs: how long after the first failure did the last distinct failure arrive, and how much wall time followed it."  # 4c72
